Spec: Private Agent transport connector

Purpose:
  Route the owned frpc control/work transport through the actual parent Agent instead of reading device keys.

Owns:
  ./linkgate.go
  ./linkgate_windows.go
  ./linkgate_unix.go
  ./linkgate_other.go
  ./linkgate_test.go

Must:
  Select bridge mode when either Agent pipe or PID metadata is present; invalid or incomplete metadata fails closed without network fallback.
  Require a TCP configuration without proxy URL and create a nonempty unpredictable initial RunID before login.
  Use the pinned Microsoft pipe library on Windows, hold the parent process through each connection and verify the actual pipe server PID before FRP bytes.
  Use a private Unix socket with verified parent PID and UID on supported Unix/Android targets; unsupported platforms fail explicitly.
  Never export or load an Agent device private key; the Agent supplies the authenticated outer TLS and fixed application scope.
